## 1. Mission

You are migrating an internal Node.js **wrapper/framework package** (a shared library other services depend on) from **Express 4 + `routing-controllers` 0.11.3 + `typedi`** to **Hono 4.x, function-based, running on Node.js via `@hono/node-server`**, with the explicit goal of **higher request throughput and a lighter dependency footprint**. As part of this you will **remove the decorator-based routing/param/DI model entirely** and replace it with plain Hono route handlers and middleware. There is **no dependency-injection container in the target state** — request-scoped state moves to `AsyncLocalStorage`, and everything else becomes plain modules/factories.

This is **not** a driver swap. `routing-controllers` does not support Hono, so its decorator/metadata layer is being deleted, not re-pointed. Treat this as a rewrite of the HTTP, validation, and middleware layers while **preserving the package's external behavior and the wire contract of every endpoint**.

### Current stack (verify against the repo)
- HTTP: `express@^4.21.2`
- Routing/DI: `routing-controllers@0.11.3`, `typedi@0.8.0`, `reflect-metadata`, `require-all`
- Custom decorators: `@ReqPathParam`, `@ReqQueryParam`, `@ReqHeaderParam` (and likely `@Req`, `@Res`, `@Body`, controller decorators), plus custom validators (`FutureDate`, `BetweenDates`, `PastDate`, `ValidDate`) and `WebSocketDecorators`
- Custom middleware classes: `ContextMiddleware`, `TimeoutMiddleware`, a request/logging middleware, `NoCacheMiddleware`
- GraphQL: `@apollo/server@4.13.0` — **note: Apollo Server 4 is EOL as of Jan 2026; this migration is also an implicit upgrade to Apollo Server 5**, which requires Node ≥20.0.0
- WebSockets / streaming: `ws@8.x`, plus an `SSE.ts`
- Validation: `class-validator@^0.14.3`
- Express middleware: `express-rate-limit`, `express-slow-down`, `express-timeout-handler`, `helmet`, `cors`, `compression`, `morgan`, `nocache`, `raw-body`
- Observability: full OpenTelemetry stack (`@opentelemetry/sdk-node`, `auto-instrumentations-node`, metrics/resources/semantic-conventions), `elastic-apm-node`, `prom-client`
- Utilities (framework-agnostic, keep as-is): `decimal.js`, `dayjs`, `json-bigint`, `http-status-codes`
- TypeScript 5.5.4, `ts-node`, dual-publish concerns (see §6.13)

