## 3. Operating principles

- **Inspect first.** Before migrating any area, read the corresponding source files end-to-end. The decorator and middleware names above are a guide; the repo is authoritative.
- **Preserve, then optimize.** First reach behavioral parity; only then apply Hono-idiomatic refactors. Don't do both in the same commit.
- **Phase by route group.** Migrate one controller/resource at a time behind contract tests. Keep the suite green at every step.
- **Compose, don't autoload.** Hono has no autoload/globbing plugin equivalent to `@fastify/autoload` or `require-all`. Each former controller becomes a module exporting a `Hono` sub-app or route-registration function, and a top-level file explicitly composes them with `app.route(prefix, subApp)`. Keep this composition file as the single source of truth for the route tree — resist the temptation to re-invent auto-discovery.
- **One commit per concern, with the contract tests that prove parity.**

