## 4. Phased plan

1. **Scaffold & bootstrap.** Stand up a `Hono` instance served via `@hono/node-server`'s `serve()`, wire the global middleware (`hono/secure-headers`, `hono/cors`, `hono/compress`, rate limiting), set up the error handler (`app.onError`), and confirm the OTel/APM init ordering (§6.10). No routes yet. Bump `engines.node` in `package.json` per §2.2.
2. **Public API inventory.** Enumerate what the package exports from its entry point(s) and which of those are decorator-based (and therefore breaking). Produce the new function-based public surface and a breaking-change list for a **major version bump** (§8).
3. **Cross-cutting layer.** Port the custom middleware classes to Hono middleware functions (§6.3), set up request context via `AsyncLocalStorage` (§6.4), logging + redaction (§6.9), and the error-shape contract (§6.8).
4. **Validation layer.** Settle the schema library (TypeBox or Zod — this is an **open decision**, not preset; see §9) and port the custom validators (§6.2).
5. **Routes, group by group.** Convert each controller to a module of function handlers with full request/response validation (§6.1). Contract-test each before moving on.
6. **GraphQL.** Integrate Apollo Server 5 via the community `apollo-server-integration-hono` package (§6.6).
7. **WebSockets & SSE.** Port via `@hono/node-ws` and a streaming route (§6.7).
8. **Decommission.** Remove `routing-controllers`, `typedi`, `reflect-metadata`, `require-all`, all `express*` packages, `morgan`, `nocache`. Confirm no `import 'reflect-metadata'` or decorator metadata remains anywhere in the codebase.
9. **Verify.** Full contract suite, load/throughput comparison vs. the Express baseline, observability smoke test, dual CJS+ESM build check on the new Node floor.

